.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt GETTYTAB 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm gettytab
.Nd terminal descriptions for getty
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The file
.Pa /etc/gettytab
describes how
.Xr getty 8
sets up a terminal line.
It is a
.Xr getcap 3
database: each record is a list of names separated by
.Ql | ,
followed by capabilities separated by
.Ql \&: .
A string capability is written
.Ar cap Ns = Ns Ar value ,
a number
.Ar cap Ns # Ns Ar value ,
and a flag is its bare name.
.Cm tc Ns = Ns Ar name
continues the record with another.
A capability missing from a record takes its value from the
.Dq default
record, and a
.Ar type
with no record uses
.Dq default
itself.
.Pp
The capabilities are:
.Bl -column "Name" "Type" "/usr/bin/login"
.It Sy Name Ta Sy Type Ta Sy Default Ta Sy Description
.It al Ta str Ta Ta log this user in automatically
.It ap Ta bool Ta false Ta any parity (7 bits, no parity check)
.It ce Ta bool Ta false Ta a CRT: erase wipes the character
.It ck Ta bool Ta false Ta a CRT: kill wipes the line
.It cl Ta str Ta Ta clear-screen sequence, sent before the banner
.It ep Ta bool Ta false Ta even parity
.It er Ta str Ta Ta erase character
.It et Ta str Ta Ta end-of-file character
.It hc Ta bool Ta false Ta do not hang up the line when it is last closed
.It ht Ta bool Ta false Ta the terminal has hardware tabs
.It if Ta str Ta Ta file whose contents are the banner
.It im Ta str Ta see below Ta the banner
.It in Ta str Ta Ta interrupt character
.It kl Ta str Ta Ta kill character
.It lm Ta str Ta login:\ Ta the login prompt
.It ln Ta str Ta Ta literal-next character
.It lo Ta str Ta /usr/bin/login Ta the program to run
.It nx Ta str Ta Ta the record to switch to on a break
.It op Ta bool Ta false Ta odd parity
.It qu Ta str Ta Ta quit character
.It rp Ta str Ta Ta reprint character
.It sa Ta str Ta Ta start character
.It sp Ta num Ta Ta line speed
.It st Ta str Ta Ta stop character
.It su Ta str Ta Ta suspend character
.It to Ta num Ta 0 Ta seconds to wait for a name
.It tt Ta str Ta Ta the terminal type, passed on as
.Ev TERM
.It we Ta str Ta Ta word-erase character
.El
.Pp
The default banner shows the system, the machine, the host name and the
terminal.
The escapes that
.Cm if ,
.Cm im
and
.Cm lm
may use are described in
.Xr getty 8 .
Characters left unset keep the 4.4BSD defaults.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/gettytab -compact
.It Pa /etc/gettytab
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getcap 3 ,
.Xr termios 4 ,
.Xr ttys 5 ,
.Xr getty 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
file appeared in
.Bx 4.1 .
